From: Noswad <64293615+TheNoswad@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 14:05:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] egl: import 16-bit Bayer as GR88, not RG88

The unpacked Bayer shaders read the low byte of each 16-bit sample from
.r and the high byte from .g, the same layout the glTexImage2D(GL_RG,
GL_UNSIGNED_BYTE) upload fallback produces. In DRM fourcc notation
(little-endian) that is DRM_FORMAT_GR88; DRM_FORMAT_RG88 has R in the
high byte.

Mesa's panfrost does not list RG88 for dma-buf import at all, so every
input buffer import failed and the software ISP mapped and uploaded each
frame from the CPU (Pixel 6 front camera, 3280x2464: ~56 ms per frame).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/src/libcamera/egl.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/egl.cpp
@@ -180,7 +180,13 @@
 		drm_format = DRM_FORMAT_R8;
 		break;
 	case GL_RG:
-		drm_format = DRM_FORMAT_RG88;
+		/*
+		 * Two bytes per texel, R from the first (low) byte: that is
+		 * GR88 in DRM's little-endian notation. RG88 has R in the high
+		 * byte, which panfrost doesn't import and other drivers would
+		 * sample byte-swapped.
+		 */
+		drm_format = DRM_FORMAT_GR88;
 		break;
 	case GL_RGBA:
 		drm_format = DRM_FORMAT_ARGB8888;
